{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '245,294p' paper.tex; sed -n '294,338p' paper.tex; cat global_memory_summary.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n\\clearpage\n\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n\\subsection{Inspectable Implementation and Reproducibility}\nThe accompanying source snapshots are readable evidence, not merely hashes identifying an unavailable implementation. \\texttt{source\\_evidence/selected\\_method.py} contains the evaluated estimator; \\texttt{source\\_evidence/evaluate\\_final.py} contains the evaluator and local references. The entrypoint manifest and method description are preserved alongside them. Table~\\ref{tab:locations} gives relevant locations. The estimator is a finite JSON request handler: reset, source transfer, source fitting, prefix observation, and release. It receives binary matrices and opaque source-group labels, not benchmark names or target identities. Predictions are bounded finite scores. Identical observed rows follow the same prediction calculation; reset and release clear learned state.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/program_spec.toml]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected_method.py#L290-L370]]\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\\small\n\\caption{Readable source locations for implementation and protocol claims. Locations refer to the supplied snapshots.}\n\\label{tab:locations}\n\\begin{tabular}{ll}\n\\toprule\nMechanism & File and lines\\\\\n\\midrule\nGroup weighting and score-targeted selection & \\texttt{selected\\_method.py}, 52--91\\\\\nRidge and difficulty fitting & \\texttt{selected\\_method.py}, 94--115\\\\\nProfiles, priors, posterior score & \\texttt{selected\\_method.py}, 118--191\\\\\nSource-only tuning and final fitting & \\texttt{selected\\_method.py}, 194--287\\\\\nModel-group split and local references & \\texttt{evaluate\\_final.py}, 685--771\\\\\nScored aggregate and paired fallback & \\texttt{evaluate\\_final.py}, 1005--1076\\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\\paragraph{Rebuilding the paper, not rerunning the evaluation.}\nThe command \\texttt{python build\\_paper\\_artifacts.py} reads only the frozen evidence registry and regenerates \\texttt{derived\\_results.json}, both quantitative figures, their PDF/PNG exports, and the numerical supplementary tables. Adjacent provenance sidecars identify the inputs. It does not execute the estimator, refit references, query language models, or rerun the sealed assessment. The overview is rendered separately; the rebuild script never overwrites an existing overview. The exact local writing environment and validation commands are documented in \\texttt{REPRODUCIBILITY.md}. The original end-to-end environment and a verified full-evaluation runtime are not established by this artifact-only reconstruction; no estimated runtime is presented as a measurement.\n% @evidence[[build_paper_artifacts.py]]\n\n\\paragraph{Data version and limits of reconstruction.}\nThe task identifies the pinned binary response-matrix snapshot \\texttt{55faff496947789f94e6b5908c77cbc3e84f81ad}. The actual evaluated objects are the staged, filtered matrices described in \\texttt{source\\_evidence/final\\_data\\_manifest.json}, not a new download from a moving leaderboard. Its group rule combines recorded base-model relations, aliases/details identities, broad family metadata, and provider fallback. Metadata cannot prove complete lineage separation. Reproducing the evaluation from upstream data requires the staged column alignment and grouping resources as well as the estimator; the frozen predictions alone are sufficient only for the paper's descriptive reaggregation. The original upstream code repository was not accessed during writing under the task's literature restriction.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/final_data_manifest.json]]\n\n\\subsection{Extended Estimation Details}\nDifficulty initialization uses the group-weighted mean ability minus the logit item mean. Item means are clipped to $[10^{-4},1-10^{-4}]$ for this initialization. Eight Newton updates use group-weighted Bernoulli residuals with difficulty penalty $0.01$ and clip each update to $[-2,2]$. Abilities remain fixed; this is not joint maximum-likelihood Rasch fitting. Profile probabilities are clipped with $\\epsilon=10^{-6}$ before applying offsets. Chunked particle summaries avoid retaining the full particle-by-item array during source tuning; a nonzero final blend stores the fitted particle probabilities. A zero blend bypasses that branch at prediction time.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected_method.py#L103-L155]]\n\nThe source folds rebuild the selected order, Rasch probabilities, profiles, and priors on each fold's training groups. Linear configurations are chosen separately for each budget using equal-group squared error. The profile/blend grid uses MAE averaged over budgets, then rows within groups, then groups. It shares the validation folds with linear tuning, so this score is not an untouched outer-fold performance estimate. If only one source group is supplied, grouped tuning is unavailable and the code uses ridge strength one, shrinkage one, and a zero profile blend. This fallback is a code-defined behavior, not evidence that the final evaluator used a single-group fit.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected_method.py#L194-L287]]\n\nEquation~\\ref{eq:profile} explicitly separates known and predicted items. In the batch path, the expected unqueried total is computed as each particle's full expected total minus its queried expected total. The single-row path sums over an explicit unqueried mask. Both implement the same algebra. This source inspection supports an implementation description, not an empirical guarantee that every execution path passed the evaluator's controls. The final diagnostic failures remain in force.\n\n\\subsection{Local Reference Implementations}\nThe anchor reference centers each item's source response vector, normalizes its length, and applies $k$-means with $k=b$, one initialization, and at most 30 iterations. Representatives are distinct nearest response vectors. Every item is reassigned to its nearest representative and representative weights are the fractions assigned. Target score prediction is the weighted average of queried responses. This reference need not match the preprocessing, optimization, or benchmark regime of published Anchor Points.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L711-L729]]\n\nThe IRT reference models logits as $\\theta_i\\exp(\\eta_j)-d_j$. Its objective is summed Bernoulli negative log likelihood plus penalties $0.5\\|\\theta\\|^2+0.05\\|\\eta\\|^2+0.005\\|d\\|^2$. L-BFGS-B uses bounded parameters and at most 40 iterations. Item order is the decreasing fitted information $a_j^2 p_j(1-p_j)$ at zero ability, where $a_j=\\exp(\\eta_j)$. Target abilities use up to 30 regularized Newton updates on queried responses; the reference score averages fitted response probabilities over the entire item universe. Finite-objective checks do not prove solver optimality. No exact reproduction of a published IRT benchmark-compression package is claimed.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L732-L771]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L732-L771]]\n\n\\subsection{Available-Pair Numerical Results}\nTable~\\ref{tab:cases_si} retains exact case-level descriptive means to more precision than the main text. All methods within a row use the same supported seeds and give equal weight to each budget and target within a seed. The table is not an extrapolation to absent records. In particular, the Commonsense row is a single split, and cannot quantify its between-seed stability.\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Conditional MAE on common available support. $n$ counts supported seeds.}\n\\label{tab:cases_si}\n\\begin{tabular}{lrrrrr}\n\\toprule\nCase & $n$ & Score design & Uniform + fit & Anchor & IRT\\\\\n\\midrule\n% BEGIN GENERATED case_mae\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\nBBH & 3 & 0.0308 & 0.0570 & 0.1551 & 0.0507 \\\\\nGPQA & 3 & 0.0128 & 0.0197 & 0.0694 & 0.0530 \\\\\nMuSR & 3 & 0.0198 & 0.0266 & 0.4441 & 0.0515 \\\\\nOL-Math & 3 & 0.0123 & 0.0221 & 0.0242 & 0.0132 \\\\\nCommonsense & 1 & 0.0455 & 0.0605 & 0.0818 & 0.1157 \\\\\nGSM & 3 & 0.0517 & 0.0590 & 0.1027 & 0.1275 \\\\\nLegalBench & 3 & 0.0440 & 0.0599 & 0.2031 & 0.0738 \\\\\nMATH & 3 & 0.0603 & 0.0624 & 0.0838 & 0.1083 \\\\\nMedQA & 3 & 0.0574 & 0.0530 & 0.2492 & 0.0845 \\\\\nMMLU & 3 & 0.0474 & 0.0634 & 0.2738 & 0.0721 \\\\\n% END GENERATED case_mae\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n% @evidence[[derived_results.json#/case_mae]]\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Conditional budget summaries. Cases receive equal weight within source domain, domains equal weight, and available seeds equal weight within case. Raw selected means and reconstructed scores use the same primary prefixes.}\n\\label{tab:budget_si}\n\\begin{tabular}{rlrr}\n\\toprule\nItems & Method & MAE & Spearman\\\\\n\\midrule\n% BEGIN GENERATED budget_metrics\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n8 & Score design & 0.0439 & 0.7787 \\\\\n8 & Uniform + fit & 0.0598 & 0.5892 \\\\\n8 & Selected mean & 0.1321 & 0.7806 \\\\\n8 & Uniform mean & 0.1082 & 0.5303 \\\\\n16 & Score design & 0.0333 & 0.8485 \\\\\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Lineage-Held-Out Anchor-Audit Residual Estimation. gate=updated; trigger=b; reason=Supplied identity and explicit ancestry metadata enable an auditable grouped stress-test category absent from the empty conclusions.\n  - evidence: Mounted README documents repeated identities/details repositories, explicit Base Model metadata, verified columns, and no provided groups or scores. Bootstrap manifest reports correct=true and combined_score=0.9414127869558047; named candidate source path was unavailable. No new experiment or score. Considered richer IRT-only prediction, pure random sampling, and protocol-only work; selected a bounded source-prediction plus uniform-residual-audit intervention with conditional unbiasedness only at the raw full-correction endpoint.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-13T17:17:14.928338+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.9444775970444405, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"anchor_mae\": 0.24719956291422063, \"combined_score\": 0.9444775970444405, \"constant_mae\": 0.2100909190340938, \"control_failure_rate\": 0.0, \"copy_mae\": 0.1778997763664952, \"correct\": false, \"delta_anchor_ci_high\": 1.0, \"delta_anchor_ci_low\": -1.0, \"delta_anchor_mae\": -0.19167715995866108, \"irt_mae\": 0.04121063683083198, \"kendall_tau_b\": 0.6472179218700796, \"mae\": 0.05552240295555956, \"missing_episode_rate\": 0.0, \"no_calibration_mae\": 0.11230918829448545, \"no_diversity_mae\": 0.060846081878834724, \"permuted_mae\": 0.1294150243149829, \"reset_mae\": 0.04647316766485056, \"reset_max_abs_error\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.06878752313066207, \"source_mean_mae\": 0.12786232844772225, \"spearman\": 0.8092089396608806, \"uniform_mae\": 0.09894661693226534}\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Score-Targeted Covariance Design with Group-Held-Out Calibration: direct full-score conditional-variance acquisition, equal source-group training weights, and source-only nested calibration. gate=updated; trigger=d; reason=Qualify the ancestry-stress-test recommendation to distinguish offline metadata from the documented opaque-source-group-only candidate interface, and distinguish recorded aggregate underperformance against IRT from an unknown acceptance-failure cause.\n  - evidence: Historical interface memory documents opaque source_groups, nested 8/16/32 prefixes, and no target full scores or target groups. Historical candidate MAE=0.05552240295555956 versus reported IRT MAE=0.04121063683083198; calibration/diversity ablations were numerically worse. Historical combined_score=0.9444775970444405 with correct=false did not establish acceptance or its failure cause; accepted bootstrap remains combined_score=0.9414127869558047 with correct=true. Considered another residual audit, richer latent reconstruction, protocol-only changes, and direct score-risk acquisition; selected the last as a bounded observable-only mechanism admitting a same-predictor D-optimal ablation. No new computation, measurement, or forbidden literature access.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-13T17:35:03.901393+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.9649669664663327, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"anchor_mae\": 0.24719956291422063, \"combined_score\": 0.9649669664663327, \"constant_mae\": 0.19445070209615578, \"control_failure_rate\": 0.0, \"copy_mae\": 0.19343264686385855, \"correct\": false, \"delta_anchor_ci_high\": 1.0, \"delta_anchor_ci_low\": -1.0, \"delta_anchor_mae\": -0.2121665293805533, \"irt_mae\": 0.04121063683083198, \"kendall_tau_b\": 0.720911927988862, \"mae\": 0.0350330335336673, \"missing_episode_rate\": 0.0, \"no_calibration_mae\": 0.03464729153264736, \"no_diversity_mae\": 0.05351526989144261, \"permuted_mae\": 0.12148785819970097, \"reset_mae\": 0.03602846597539919, \"reset_max_abs_error\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.04484693916622435, \"source_mean_mae\": 0.12786232844772225, \"spearman\": 0.8644226555576705, \"uniform_mae\": 0.09894661693226534}\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Rasch-Residual Profile Mixtures on Fixed Score-Targeted Prefixes. gate=updated; trigger=b; reason=Add the untested nonlinear residual-profile posterior category while retaining the existing source-only acquisition and evidence restrictions.\n  - evidence: Historical cycle-2 MAE 0.0350330335336673 versus IRT 0.04121063683083198; no-calibration 0.03464729153264736 and no-diversity 0.05351526989144261. Acceptance was not established and its cause remains unknown. No new experiment. Considered repeated auditing, adaptive posterior acquisition, and calibration-only changes; selected a matched-prefix estimator intervention requiring no new observations. Hypothesis: group-balanced Rasch-shrunk source profiles and ability offsets can complement the linear predictor; model-based posterior spread is not target-calibrated uncertainty.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-13T17:51:56.142148+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.9684365684559878, correct=True; scientific acceptance passed; search metrics (data): {\"anchor_mae\": 0.24719956291422063, \"combined_score\": 0.9684365684559878, \"constant_mae\": 0.2040049293753487, \"control_failure_rate\": 0.0, \"copy_mae\": 0.19502341674926077, \"correct\": true, \"delta_anchor_ci_high\": 1.0, \"delta_anchor_ci_low\": -1.0, \"delta_anchor_mae\": -0.21563613137020848, \"irt_mae\": 0.04121063683083198, \"kendall_tau_b\": 0.75310530481357, \"mae\": 0.031563431544012165, \"missing_episode_rate\": 0.0, \"no_calibration_mae\": 0.12348718192012596, \"no_diversity_mae\": 0.05351873980080848, \"permuted_mae\": 0.12275843002570605, \"reset_mae\": 0.026756557227656522, \"reset_max_abs_error\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.041163281675283644, \"source_mean_mae\": 0.12786232844772225, \"spearman\": 0.8878296042522897, \"uniform_mae\": 0.09894661693226534}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
