{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat global_memory/conclusions.md; sed -n '1,130p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; sed -n '200,213p' paper.tex; sed -n '289,311p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,24p' global_memory_summary.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat global_memory/conclusions.md; sed -n '1,130p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; sed -n '200,213p' paper.tex; sed -n '289,311p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,24p' global_memory_summary.md\"","aggregated_output":"Scope grouping claims to the interface: use supplied opaque source groups for leakage-controlled validation; reserve identity/explicit-ancestry stress tests for authorized offline metadata, and never infer lineage from architecture or invent ancestry. Retain source-only benchmark-mean conditional-covariance acquisition as a lead, with same-predictor D-optimal and strong IRT controls. Explore a group-balanced mixture of Rasch-shrunk source response profiles with ability offsets as an untested nonlinear estimator on identical fixed prefixes; use grouped tuning with a zero-weight linear fallback to isolate estimator complementarity. Treat offsets as global-strength extrapolation, not protection against unseen skills, and do not interpret posterior concentration as calibrated target uncertainty. Test calibration and group weighting separately, refitting acquisition and all profile/prior fitting inside grouped source folds. Historical aggregate method differences do not establish paired causal effects or explain failed acceptance; source-tuned gains and post-selection uncertainty are not independent target evidence. If revisiting a uniform-complement residual audit, reserve conditional design-unbiasedness for its frozen-predictor, full-correction, unclipped endpoint, not shrinkage or clipped variants. Compare paired equal-budget methods with group-level uncertainty before claiming improvement; no accepted improvement has been established. Respect absent target full scores and target group identities, keep diagnostics internal, and report inaccessible experiments as incomplete without weakening scientific or paper requirements. Unavailable incumbent source and correct=false alone are not evidence of an implementation defect.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef _markdown_entry(event: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Handle markdown entry logic for this module.\"\"\"\n    lines = [\n        f\"### {event['timestamp']} | step={event['step']} | scope={event['scope']}\",\n        f\"- summary: {event['summary']}\",\n        f\"- evidence: {event['evidence']}\",\n        f\"- next_action: {event['next_action']}\",\n    ]\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = event.get(key)\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value.strip():\n            lines.append(f\"- {key}: {value.strip()}\")\n\n    metrics = event.get(\"metrics\")\n    if isinstance(metrics, dict) and metrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- metrics: {json.dumps(metrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    rubrics = event.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if isinstance(rubrics, list) and rubrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- rubrics: {json.dumps(rubrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    tags = event.get(\"tags\")\n    if isinstance(tags, list) and tags:\n        lines.append(f\"- tags: {', '.join(str(item) for item in tags)}\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef _append_text(path: Path, text: str, *, header: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Safely initialize and append text to a regular file.\"\"\"\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if not size:\n\\end{figure}\n% @evidence[[derived_results.json#/case_seed_mae]]\n\nThe conditional comparison differs from the reported aggregate ordering because it changes both the available support and the handling of missing records. Neither view should replace the other: the reported aggregate reflects the evaluator's failure policy, while the conditional view describes retained predictions. The latter is compatible with useful prediction accuracy on observed cases and simultaneously insufficient evidence for a qualified overall result. It does not establish that missingness is benign or that the omitted outcomes would follow the same pattern.\n\n\\subsection{Item Budget, Reconstruction, and Ranking}\nOn the stated common-support aggregation, primary MAE is 0.0439, 0.0333, and 0.0278 at the three budgets; fitted uniform-selection MAE is 0.0598, 0.0439, and 0.0328. Figure~\\ref{fig:budgets} separates absolute-score prediction from model ranking. Selected-item raw means have much larger MAE (0.1321, 0.1050, and 0.0851), but Spearman correlations of 0.7806, 0.8461, and 0.8819 are close to the primary values of 0.7787, 0.8485, and 0.8858. Reconstruction therefore changes absolute-score error much more than rank correlation in this retained evidence. This is a descriptive matched-order contrast, not an attribution to any one reconstruction component.\n% @evidence[[derived_results.json#/budget_mae]]\n% @evidence[[derived_results.json#/budget_spearman]]\n\n\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{figures/budget_accuracy_and_ranking.pdf}\n\\caption{Conditional error and ranking at each budget. Large dots use equal data-source and case weights, with available seeds normalized within each case. Small dots are descriptive seed summaries normalized over cases available for that seed; they are not independent replicates of the pooled estimator. Both panels and all methods use the same available case--seed intersection. No confidence interval or qualified overall comparison is implied.}\n\\subsection{Local Reference Implementations}\nThe anchor reference centers each item's source response vector, normalizes its length, and applies $k$-means with $k=b$, one initialization, and at most 30 iterations. Representatives are distinct nearest response vectors. Every item is reassigned to its nearest representative and representative weights are the fractions assigned. Target score prediction is the weighted average of queried responses. This reference need not match the preprocessing, optimization, or benchmark regime of published Anchor Points.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L711-L729]]\n\nThe IRT reference models logits as $\\theta_i\\exp(\\eta_j)-d_j$. Its objective is summed Bernoulli negative log likelihood plus penalties $0.5\\|\\theta\\|^2+0.05\\|\\eta\\|^2+0.005\\|d\\|^2$. L-BFGS-B uses bounded parameters and at most 40 iterations. Item order is the decreasing fitted information $a_j^2 p_j(1-p_j)$ at zero ability, where $a_j=\\exp(\\eta_j)$. Target abilities use up to 30 regularized Newton updates on queried responses; the reference score averages fitted response probabilities over the entire item universe. Finite-objective checks do not prove solver optimality. No exact reproduction of a published IRT benchmark-compression package is claimed.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L732-L771]]\n\n\\subsection{Available-Pair Numerical Results}\nTable~\\ref{tab:cases_si} retains exact case-level descriptive means to more precision than the main text. All methods within a row use the same supported seeds and give equal weight to each budget and target within a seed. The table is not an extrapolation to absent records. In particular, the Commonsense row is a single split, and cannot quantify its between-seed stability.\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Conditional MAE on common available support. $n$ counts supported seeds.}\n\\label{tab:cases_si}\n\\begin{tabular}{lrrrrr}\n\\toprule\nCase & $n$ & Score design & Uniform + fit & Anchor & IRT\\\\\n\\midrule\n% BEGIN GENERATED case_mae\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\nBBH & 3 & 0.0308 & 0.0570 & 0.1551 & 0.0507 \\\\\nGPQA & 3 & 0.0128 & 0.0197 & 0.0694 & 0.0530 \\\\\nMuSR & 3 & 0.0198 & 0.0266 & 0.4441 & 0.0515 \\\\\nOL-Math & 3 & 0.0123 & 0.0221 & 0.0242 & 0.0132 \\\\\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Lineage-Held-Out Anchor-Audit Residual Estimation. gate=updated; trigger=b; reason=Supplied identity and explicit ancestry metadata enable an auditable grouped stress-test category absent from the empty conclusions.\n  - evidence: Mounted README documents repeated identities/details repositories, explicit Base Model metadata, verified columns, and no provided groups or scores. Bootstrap manifest reports correct=true and combined_score=0.9414127869558047; named candidate source path was unavailable. No new experiment or score. Considered richer IRT-only prediction, pure random sampling, and protocol-only work; selected a bounded source-prediction plus uniform-residual-audit intervention with conditional unbiasedness only at the raw full-correction endpoint.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-13T17:17:14.928338+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.9444775970444405, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"anchor_mae\": 0.24719956291422063, \"combined_score\": 0.9444775970444405, \"constant_mae\": 0.2100909190340938, \"control_failure_rate\": 0.0, \"copy_mae\": 0.1778997763664952, \"correct\": false, \"delta_anchor_ci_high\": 1.0, \"delta_anchor_ci_low\": -1.0, \"delta_anchor_mae\": -0.19167715995866108, \"irt_mae\": 0.04121063683083198, \"kendall_tau_b\": 0.6472179218700796, \"mae\": 0.05552240295555956, \"missing_episode_rate\": 0.0, \"no_calibration_mae\": 0.11230918829448545, \"no_diversity_mae\": 0.060846081878834724, \"permuted_mae\": 0.1294150243149829, \"reset_mae\": 0.04647316766485056, \"reset_max_abs_error\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.06878752313066207, \"source_mean_mae\": 0.12786232844772225, \"spearman\": 0.8092089396608806, \"uniform_mae\": 0.09894661693226534}\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Score-Targeted Covariance Design with Group-Held-Out Calibration: direct full-score conditional-variance acquisition, equal source-group training weights, and source-only nested calibration. gate=updated; trigger=d; reason=Qualify the ancestry-stress-test recommendation to distinguish offline metadata from the documented opaque-source-group-only candidate interface, and distinguish recorded aggregate underperformance against IRT from an unknown acceptance-failure cause.\n  - evidence: Historical interface memory documents opaque source_groups, nested 8/16/32 prefixes, and no target full scores or target groups. Historical candidate MAE=0.05552240295555956 versus reported IRT MAE=0.04121063683083198; calibration/diversity ablations were numerically worse. Historical combined_score=0.9444775970444405 with correct=false did not establish acceptance or its failure cause; accepted bootstrap remains combined_score=0.9414127869558047 with correct=true. Considered another residual audit, richer latent reconstruction, protocol-only changes, and direct score-risk acquisition; selected the last as a bounded observable-only mechanism admitting a same-predictor D-optimal ablation. No new computation, measurement, or forbidden literature access.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
